Z||000003||Formula88||02-18-2001||12:19 PM||||I would go with the cat-back exhaust first. You won't get much performance gain from headers feeding into factory exhaust, but the cat-back can give a decent boost without the headers.  Then, if you add the headers later, they'll be able to do some good.  ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Phil||02-18-2001||01:14 PM||||Personally I would go for brakes and suspension replacement/upgrades, but if you're bent on the exhaust do the cat back and just port your stock manifolds(almost the same gain as headers and it's free).||||reg||1
